      "problem": "Express the compound inequality $x<1$ or $x\\ge \\sqrt{2}$ using interval notation.",
      "worked_solution": "We can represent the compound inequality on a number line, as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14191664/assets/e57c442c1524bf9c62feaefb1215cdfde23fee7dbbaf4207ce2e62bc8655769b.png)\n\nThe number line consists of the interval $(-\\infty ,1)$ as well as the interval $[\\sqrt{2},\\infty ).$\n\nSo, we can express the compound inequality as the union of these two intervals:\n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,1)\\cup [\\sqrt{2},\\infty )\n$$",
